#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Isang libreng kurso ng IBM sa quantum information at computation"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deutsch's algorithm"
msgstr "Algoritmo ni Deutsch"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm solves the parity problem for the special case that $n = 1$.\n"
"In the context of quantum computing this problem is sometimes referred to as *Deutsch's problem*, and we'll follow that nomenclature in this lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang algoritmo ni Deutsch ay naglulutas ng parity problem para sa espesyal na kaso na $n = 1$.\n"
"Sa konteksto ng quantum computing, ang problemang ito ay tinutukoy minsan bilang *Deutsch's problem*, at susundin natin ang nomenclature na iyon sa araling ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be precise, the input is represented by a function $f:\\Sigma \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ from one bit to one bit.\n"
"There are four such functions:\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang maging tumpak, ang input ay kinakatawan ng isang function na $f:\\Sigma \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ mula sa isang bit patungo sa isang bit.\n"
"May apat na ganyang function:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rule[-10mm]{0mm}{10mm}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_1(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_2(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_3(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_4(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rule[-10mm]{0mm}{10mm}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_1(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_2(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_3(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_4(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first and last of these functions are *constant* and the middle two are *balanced*, meaning that the two possible output values for the function occur the same number of times as we range over the inputs.\n"
"Deutsch's problem is to determine which of these two categories the input function belongs to: constant or balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang una at huli sa mga function na ito ay *constant* at ang dalawa sa gitna ay *balanced*, ibig sabihin, ang dalawang posibleng output value ng function ay parehong dalas habang inuulit natin ang mga input.\n"
"Ang Deutsch's problem ay ang tukuyin kung alin sa dalawang kategoryang ito ang kinabibilangan ng input function: constant o balanced.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Deutsch's problem\">\n"
"Input:  a function $f:\\{0,1\\}\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Output: $0$ if $f$ is constant, $1$ if $f$ is balanced\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Deutsch's problem\">\n"
"Input:  a function $f:\\{0,1\\}\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Output: $0$ if $f$ is constant, $1$ if $f$ is balanced\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we view the input function $f$ in Deutsch's problem as representing random access to a string, we're thinking about a two-bit string: $f(0)f(1)$.\n"
msgstr "Kung titingnan natin ang input function na $f$ sa Deutsch's problem bilang random access sa isang string, iniisip natin ang isang two-bit string: $f(0)f(1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"\\mathsf{function} & \\mathsf{string}\\\\\n"
"\\hline\n"
"f_1 & 00 \\\\\n"
"f_2 & 01 \\\\\n"
"f_3 & 10 \\\\\n"
"f_4 & 11\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"\\mathsf{function} & \\mathsf{string}\\\\\n"
"\\hline\n"
"f_1 & 00 \\\\\n"
"f_2 & 01 \\\\\n"
"f_3 & 10 \\\\\n"
"f_4 & 11\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When viewed in this way, Deutsch's problem is to compute the parity (or, equivalently, the exclusive-OR) of the two bits.\n"
msgstr "Kapag tiningnan sa ganitong paraan, ang Deutsch's problem ay ang komputahin ang parity (o, katumbas nito, ang exclusive-OR) ng dalawang bit.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every classical query algorithm that correctly solves this problem must query both bits: $f(0)$ and $f(1)$.\n"
"If we learn that $f(1) = 1$, for instance, the answer could still be $0$ or $1$, depending on whether $f(0) = 1$ or $f(0) = 0$, respectively.\n"
"Every other case is similar; knowing just one of two bits doesn't provide any information at all about their parity.\n"
"So, the Boolean circuit described in the previous section is the best we can do in terms of the number of queries required to solve this problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bawat classical query algorithm na tama ang paglutas sa problemang ito ay kailangang i-query ang parehong bit: $f(0)$ at $f(1).$\n"
"Halimbawa, kung nalaman natin na $f(1) = 1,$ ang sagot ay maaari pa ring $0$ o $1,$ depende kung $f(0) = 1$ o $f(0) = 0,$ ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"
"Katulad nito ang bawat ibang kaso; ang pagkaalam ng isa lang sa dalawang bit ay walang anumang impormasyon tungkol sa kanilang parity.\n"
"Kaya, ang Boolean circuit na inilarawan sa nakaraang seksyon ang pinakamainam na magagawa natin sa bilang ng mga query na kailangan para malutas ang problemang ito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuit description {#quantum-circuit-description}"
msgstr "Paglalarawan ng quantum circuit {#quantum-circuit-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm solves Deutsch's problem using a single query, therefore providing a quantifiable advantage of quantum over classical computations.\n"
"This may be a modest advantage — one query as opposed to two — but we have to start somewhere.\n"
"Scientific advances sometimes have seemingly humble origins.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang algoritmo ni Deutsch ay naglulutas ng Deutsch's problem gamit ang isang query, kaya nagbibigay ito ng mapapanukalang kalamangan ng quantum kumpara sa classical na computation.\n"
"Maaaring humble ang kalamangan na ito — isang query kumpara sa dalawa — ngunit kailangan naming magsimula sa isang lugar.\n"
"Ang mga pag-unlad sa agham ay minsan may tila hamak na pinagmulan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a quantum circuit that describes Deutsch's algorithm:\n"
msgstr "Narito ang isang quantum circuit na naglalarawan ng algoritmo ni Deutsch:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Pagsusuri {#analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To analyze Deutsch's algorithm, we will trace through the action of the circuit above and identify the states of the qubits at the times suggested by this figure:\n"
msgstr "Para suriin ang algoritmo ni Deutsch, susubaybayan natin ang aksyon ng circuit sa itaas at tutukuyin ang mga estado ng mga qubit sa mga oras na iminumungkahi ng figure na ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![States during Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit-states.svg)\n"
msgstr "![States during Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit-states.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The initial state is $\\vert 1\\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle$, and the two Hadamard operations on the left-hand side of the circuit transform this state to\n"
msgstr "Ang paunang estado ay $\\vert 1\\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle$, at ang dalawang Hadamard operation sa kaliwang bahagi ng circuit ay nagbabago ng estadong ito sa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_1 \\rangle = \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_1 \\rangle = \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(As always, we're following Qiskit's qubit ordering convention, which puts the top qubit to the right and the bottom qubit to the left.) It may feel unintuitive to write this product state partly distributed (leaving the states of qubit 1 factored out), but this will make our later expressions more compact.\n"
msgstr "(Tulad ng lagi, sinusunod natin ang qubit ordering convention ng Qiskit, na naglalagay ng pinakamataas na qubit sa kanan at ang pinakamababang qubit sa kaliwa.) Maaaring hindi natural ang pagsusulat ng product state na ito nang bahagyang ipinagkalat (na iniiwan ang mga estado ng qubit 1 na naka-factor out), ngunit gagawin nitong mas maayos ang ating mga susunod na expression.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, the $U_f$ gate is performed.\n"
"According to the definition of the $U_f$ gate, the value of the function $f$ for the classical state of the top/rightmost qubit is XORed onto the bottom/leftmost qubit, which transforms $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ into the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, isasagawa ang gate na $U_f$.\n"
"Ayon sa kahulugan ng gate na $U_f$, ang halaga ng function na $f$ para sa classical state ng pinakamataas/pinakakanang qubit ay XOR-ed sa pinakamababa/pinakakaliwang qubit, na nagbabago ng $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ sa estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can simplify this expression by observing that the formula\n"
msgstr "Maaari nating pasimplehin ang expression na ito sa pamamagitan ng pagmamasid na ang formula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus a\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus a\\rangle = (-1)^a \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus a\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus a\\rangle = (-1)^a \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"works for both possible values $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"More explicitly, the two cases are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"ay gumagana para sa parehong posibleng halaga na $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Mas malinaw, ang dalawang kaso ay ang mga sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 0\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 0\\rangle\n"
"& = \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^0 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 1\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 1\\rangle & = \\vert 1 \\rangle - \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^1 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 0\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 0\\rangle\n"
"& = \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^0 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 1\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 1\\rangle & = \\vert 1 \\rangle - \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^1 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we can alternatively express $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$ like this:\n"
msgstr "Kaya, maaari nating ilarawan ang $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$ nang ganito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(0)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(1)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(0)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(1)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Something interesting just happened!\n"
"Although the action of the $U_f$ gate on standard basis states leaves the top/rightmost qubit alone and XORs the function value onto the bottom/leftmost qubit, here we see that the state of the top/rightmost qubit has changed (in general) while the state of the bottom/leftmost qubit remains the same — specifically being in the $\\vert - \\rangle$ state before and after the $U_f$ gate is performed.\n"
"This phenomenon is known as the *phase kickback*, and we will have more to say about it shortly.\n"
msgstr ""
"May nangyaring kagiliw-giliw na bagay!\n"
"Bagama't ang aksyon ng gate na $U_f$ sa standard basis states ay nag-iiwan ng pinakamataas/pinakakanang qubit nang walang pagbabago at XOR-s ang halaga ng function sa pinakamababa/pinakakaliwang qubit, makikita natin dito na nagbago ang estado ng pinakamataas/pinakakanang qubit (sa pangkalahatan) habang nananatiling pareho ang estado ng pinakamababa/pinakakaliwang qubit — lalo na nasa estado $\\vert - \\rangle$ bago at pagkatapos na isagawa ang gate na $U_f$.\n"
"Ang penomenong ito ay kilala bilang *phase kickback*, at magkakaroon pa tayo ng mas maraming sasabihin tungkol dito sa lalong madaling panahon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With one final simplification, which is to pull the factor of $(-1)^{f(0)}$ outside of the sum, we obtain this expression of the state $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$:\n"
msgstr "Sa isang huling pagpapasimple, na ang pag-alis ng factor na $(-1)^{f(0)}$ mula sa loob ng sum, makukuha natin ang expression na ito ng estado $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"      \\biggl( \\frac{\\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(0) \\oplus f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert - \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$}.\n"
"      \\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"      \\biggl( \\frac{\\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(0) \\oplus f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert - \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$}.\n"
"      \\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that in this expression, we have $f(0) \\oplus f(1)$ in the exponent of $-1$ as opposed to $f(1) - f(0)$, which is what we might expect from a purely algebraic viewpoint, but we obtain the same result either way.\n"
"This is because the value $(-1)^k$ for any integer $k$ depends only on whether $k$ is even or odd.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pansinin na sa expression na ito, mayroon tayong $f(0) \\oplus f(1)$ sa exponent ng $-1$ kumpara sa $f(1) - f(0)$, na maaaring inaasahan natin mula sa isang purong algebraic na pananaw, ngunit pareho ang resulta sa dalawang paraan.\n"
"Ito ay dahil ang halaga ng $(-1)^k$ para sa anumang integer na $k$ ay nakasalalay lamang sa kung ang $k$ ay even o odd.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the final Hadamard gate to the top qubit leaves us with the state\n"
msgstr "Ang pagsasagawa ng huling Hadamard gate sa pinakamataas na qubit ay nagbibigay sa atin ng estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_3 \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$},\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_3 \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$},\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which leads to the correct outcome with probability $1$ when the right/topmost qubit is measured.\n"
msgstr "na nagdudulot ng tamang resulta na may probabilidad na $1$ kapag sinukat ang kanan/pinakamataas na qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Further remarks on the phase kickback {#further-remarks-on-the-phase-kickback}"
msgstr "Karagdagang puna tungkol sa phase kickback {#further-remarks-on-the-phase-kickback}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before moving on, let's look at the analysis above from a slightly different angle that may shed some light on the phase kickback phenomenon.\n"
msgstr "Bago magpatuloy, tingnan natin ang pagsusuri sa itaas mula sa bahagyang ibang anggulo na maaaring magbigay-liwanag sa penomenon ng phase kickback.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, notice that the following formula works for all choices of bits $b,c\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
msgstr "Una, pansinin na ang sumusunod na formula ay gumagana para sa lahat ng pagpili ng mga bit na $b,c\\in\\Sigma$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus c\\rangle = X^c \\vert b \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus c\\rangle = X^c \\vert b \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This can be verified by checking it for the two possible values $c = 0$ and $c = 1$:\n"
msgstr "Maaari itong mapatunayan sa pamamagitan ng pagsusuri nito para sa dalawang posibleng halaga na $c = 0$ at $c = 1$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 0 \\rangle & = \\vert b\\rangle = \\mathbb{I} \\vert b \\rangle = X^0 \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 1 \\rangle & = \\vert \\neg b\\rangle = X \\vert b \\rangle = X^1 \\vert b \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 0 \\rangle & = \\vert b\\rangle = \\mathbb{I} \\vert b \\rangle = X^0 \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 1 \\rangle & = \\vert \\neg b\\rangle = X \\vert b \\rangle = X^1 \\vert b \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using this formula, we see that\n"
msgstr "Gamit ang formula na ito, makikita natin na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl(\\vert b\\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert b \\oplus f(a) \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert b \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl(\\vert b\\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert b \\oplus f(a) \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert b \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for every choice of bits $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Because this formula is true for $b=0$ and $b=1$, we see by linearity that\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa bawat pagpili ng mga bit na $a,b\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
"Dahil tama ang formula na ito para sa $b=0$ at $b=1$, makikita natin sa pamamagitan ng linearity na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert \\psi \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert \\psi \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all qubit state vectors $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$, and therefore\n"
msgstr "para sa lahat ng qubit state vector na $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$, at samakatuwid\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The key that makes this work is that $X\\vert - \\rangle = - \\vert - \\rangle$.\n"
"In mathematical terms, the vector $\\vert - \\rangle$ is an *eigenvector* of the matrix $X$ having *eigenvalue* $-1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang susi na gumagana rito ay ang $X\\vert - \\rangle = - \\vert - \\rangle$.\n"
"Sa mga mathematical na termino, ang vector na $\\vert - \\rangle$ ay isang *eigenvector* ng matrix na $X$ na may *eigenvalue* na $-1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll discuss eigenvectors and eigenvalues in greater detail in the upcoming lesson on *Phase estimation and factoring,* where the phase kickback phenomenon is generalized to other unitary operations.\n"
msgstr "Tatalakayin natin ang mga eigenvector at eigenvalue nang mas detalyado sa susunod na aralin tungkol sa *Phase estimation and factoring,* kung saan ang penomenon ng phase kickback ay ginagawang mas pangkalahatan para sa iba pang unitary operation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keeping in mind that scalars float freely through tensor products, we find an alternative way of reasoning how the operation $U_f$ transforms $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ into $\\vert \\pi_2\\rangle$ in the analysis above:\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang mga scalar ay malaya na lumipat sa pamamagitan ng tensor product, makikita natin ang alternatibong paraan ng pag-iisip kung paano binabago ng operasyon $U_f$ ang $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ sa $\\vert \\pi_2\\rangle$ sa pagsusuri sa itaas:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"  & = U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"    + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"  & = U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"    + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation in Qiskit {#implementation-in-qiskit}"
msgstr "Implementasyon sa Qiskit {#implementation-in-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's see how we can implement Deutsch's algorithm in Qiskit. We'll start with a version check and then perform the imports required solely for this implementation.\n"
"For the implementations of other algorithms that follows, we'll perform the required imports separately for the sake of greater modularity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan natin ngayon kung paano natin maipapatupad ang algoritmo ni Deutsch sa Qiskit. Magsisimula tayo sa isang version check at pagkatapos ay gagawin ang mga import na kailangan para sa implementasyong ito.\n"
"Para sa mga implementasyon ng iba pang mga algorithm na susunod, gagawin natin ang mga kinakailangang import nang hiwalay para sa mas malaking modularity.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First we'll define a quantum circuit that implements a query gate for one of the four functions $f_1$, $f_2$, $f_3$, or $f_4$ from one bit to one bit described previously. As we already mentioned, the implementation of query gates is not really a part of Deutsch's algorithm itself;\n"
"here we're essentially just showing one way to prepare the input, in the form of a circuit implementation of a query gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, magtatakda tayo ng isang quantum circuit na nagpapatupad ng query gate para sa isa sa apat na function na $f_1,$ $f_2,$ $f_3,$ o $f_4$ mula sa isang bit patungo sa isang bit na inilarawan kanina. Tulad ng nabanggit na natin, ang implementasyon ng mga query gate ay hindi talaga bahagi ng algoritmo ni Deutsch mismo;\n"
"dito ay nagpapakita lang tayo ng isang paraan para ihanda ang input, sa anyo ng isang circuit implementation ng isang query gate.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can see what each circuit looks like using the `draw` method. Here's the circuit for the function $f_3$.\n"
msgstr "Maaari nating makita kung ano ang hitsura ng bawat circuit gamit ang `draw` method. Narito ang circuit para sa function na $f_3$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/787e3c81-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/787e3c81-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we will create the actual quantum circuit for Deutsch's algorithm, substituting the query gate with a quantum circuit implementation given as an argument. Shortly we'll plug in one of the four circuits defined by the function `deutsch_function` we defined earlier.\n"
"Barriers are included to show the visual separation between the query gate implementation and the rest of the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, lilikha tayo ng aktwal na quantum circuit para sa algoritmo ni Deutsch, na pinalitan ang query gate ng isang quantum circuit implementation na ibinibigay bilang argumento. Sa lalong madaling panahon ay ipa-plug natin ang isa sa apat na circuit na tinukoy ng function na `deutsch_function` na tinukoy natin kanina.\n"
"Ang mga barrier ay kasama upang ipakita ang visual na paghihiwalay sa pagitan ng query gate implementation at ng natitirang bahagi ng circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Again we can see what the circuit looks like using the `draw` method.\n"
msgstr "Muli, maaari nating makita kung ano ang hitsura ng circuit gamit ang `draw` method.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/27b41067-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-outputs/27b41067-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we'll create a function that runs the circuit previously defined one time and outputs the appropriate result: \"constant\" or \"balanced.\"\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, lilikha tayo ng isang function na nagpapatakbo ng circuit na dati nating tinukoy nang isang beses at naglalabas ng naaangkop na resulta: \"constant\" o \"balanced.\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now run Deutsch's algorithm on any one of the four functions defined above.\n"
msgstr "Maaari na nating patakbuhin ang algoritmo ni Deutsch sa anumang isa sa apat na function na tinukoy sa itaas.\n"
